rability":58.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":0.241962453694907,"_gp_fcf_durability":true,"_score_fcf_durability":100.0,"_gate_margins":0.002061683752043504,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":52.1,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07029006518160154,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":89.2,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.0015673442131464155,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":52.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0011070444173331526,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":98.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.3419,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Plains All American Pipeline, L.P., through its subsidiaries, engages in the pipeline transportation, terminalling, storage, and gathering of crude oil and natural gas liquids (NGL) in the United States and Canada. The company operates through two segments, Crude Oil and NGL. The Crude Oil segment offers gathering and transporting crude oil through pipelines, trucks, and on barges or railcars. This segment provides terminalling, storage, and other related services, as well as merchant activities. The NGL segment is involved in natural gas processing and NGL fractionation, storage, transportation, and terminaling. This segment also includes ethane, propane, normal butane, iso-butane, and natural gasoline derived from natural gas production and processing activities, as well as crude oil refining processes. Its NGL components are used for various applications, such as heating, engine, and industrial fuels. The company was founded in 1981 and is headquartered in Houston, Texas. Plains All American Pipeline, L.P. operates as a subsidiary of Plains GP Holdings, L.P.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Wilfred C.W. Chiang | President, CEO & Chairman of Plains All American GP LLC | Age 64 | Compensation: $3.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $11.3M ranks in the top quartile among Energy peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $588K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $13K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Plains All American Pipeline, L is a large-cap energy business with a $16.9B market cap on $44.3B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Gross margins of 5% are the starting point for assessing pricing power.","The business throws off $2.3B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 5 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.05\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.6\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 2.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.0% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 34% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Payout ratio looks stretched \u2014 the dividend\u2019s own margin of safety is thin","sev":"red","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Operating margins 12% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 71% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7146202253768474},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Energy peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Energy peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Energy tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Geopolitical supply shocks \u2014 wars, sanctions, and OPEC decisions create volatility that no hedging programme can fully neutralise.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 42% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","27 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Energy sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 6% over 3 months","Energy ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Plains (PAA) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/plains-paa-q3-2026-earnings-223408000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1794005059.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Plains All American narrows 2026 adjusted EBITDA guidance to $2.88B +/-$50M as it targets about 200,000 bpd Permian growth (NASDAQ:PAA)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4668469-plains-all-american-narrows-2026-adjusted-ebitda-guidance-to-2_88b-50m-as-it-targets-about","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793